id: pm-pbo502
title: "Continuous MCP upstream conformance ingestion: official specs, SEPs, extensions, schemas, SDK guidance, and roadmap changes become versioned executable work"
description: "Turn upstream MCP evolution into a repeatable project-management and release process. Each normative or roadmap change is classified against the public SDK, CLI, servers, packages, docs, tests, deprecations, and released consumers with explicit unknown and proposal states."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[7]: "area:ci","area:mcp",conformance,continuous-ingestion,roadmap,sdk,standards
created_at: "2026-08-28T20:22:36.383Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T20:58:33.569Z"
deadline: "2027-12-31T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 600
acceptance_criteria: Official sources and revisions are recorded with retrieval time and immutable content identity; normative requirements proposals and roadmap aspirations are never conflated; every changed requirement maps to one canonical owner or an explicit no-impact decision; generated matrices detect unowned SDK CLI MCP package test and documentation gaps; upstream SDK defaults and opt-ins are tested rather than inferred from package version; release gates run real transport and published-consumer scenarios with negative controls; deprecation clocks create actionable migration deadlines before removal; ingestion is incremental resumable and bounded for decades of revisions
parent: pm-opw1l3
risk: high
confidence: high
